From a50cd948fef518e7f2bee23ddf4385aa7b3fd5b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] disk_state: defer digests and cache nodes within write
 transactions

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Defer intermediate DiskStateStore branch re-hashing using an in-transaction
node_cache and avoid copying unchanged subtrees during GBT state_root computation.

Original-Commit: 8e8449da36a902436cd4fba68e071d6cde54b437
Original-Patch: v2/027
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

(cherry picked from commit 6aa5347845579f6885bd0b554a92f286aded1c2d)

Canonical-Source-Commit: 6aa5347845579f6885bd0b554a92f286aded1c2d
